The game's Map shows the land, the roads, and the villages, but not the cabins you passed, the caves, or the ore rocks you saw, so you set markers by hand to find them again. This mod draws them on the Map for you. The idea is close to [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thelastplagueblight/mods/7]Cave markers and more[/url], but the mod runs inside the game with no separate program, and it adds ore deposits, fog of war, and a legend.

[size=4][b]Main features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Cabins and caves.[/b] Icons mark the cabins and the cave entrances.[/*]
[*][b]Ore deposits.[/b] Tin, copper, iron, and silver rocks show as colored dots. Rocks inside a cave get no dot.[/*]
[*][b]Hover texts.[/b] Point at a dot to see its rock count, such as "Iron deposit (4)". A cave lists the ore inside it, such as "Iron Ore (7)".[/*]
[*][b]Fog of war.[/b] The land that you have not explored yet shows darker.[/*]
[*][b]Legend.[/b] Click a row of the legend to hide or show that kind, also the fog of war.[/*]
[*][b]Save safety.[/b] The mod writes nothing to your save, so you can remove it at any time. Single player only.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Why parts of the Map are empty[/b][/size]
Cabins and ore only show up in land you've been near. The game uses procedural generation: it generates the world around you as you explore, and the mod can't mark what isn't generated yet, so the fog of war darkens that land. Go into a dark area and open the Map again: the cabins and ore you passed are on it, and a rock you mined out is gone. Caves work differently. The game knows every cave in the region, so they show from the start.

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]The Last Plague: Blight 0.12.7 or later. Also tested on the beta branch new-save-system (game version 0.12.8b3).[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thelastplagueblight/mods/9]BepInEx for The Last Plague: Blight[/url].[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thelastplagueblight/mods/9]BepInEx[/url].[/*]
[*]Extract this mod's zip into the game folder (the folder with the game .exe). The DLL lands in BepInEx\plugins. Full path example:
[code]C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\The Last Plague\BepInEx\plugins\MapOverhaul.dll[/code][/*][/list]

[size=4][b]Uninstall[/b][/size]
Delete [font=Courier New]MapOverhaul.dll[/font] from the [font=Courier New]BepInEx\plugins[/font] folder, and the folder [font=Courier New]BepInEx\cache\MapOverhaul[/font].

[size=4][b]Configuration[/b][/size]
The legend on the Map saves its rows for you. To change mod settings by hand, edit [font=Courier New]BepInEx\config\com.ivmakk.thelastplagueblight.mapoverhaul.cfg[/font] while the game is closed (see [url=https://github.com/ivmakk-tlpb/tlpb-map-overhaul/blob/main/CONFIG.md]CONFIG.md[/url] for every setting). Changes apply at the next game start.

